\fs32\b Propentra Property Management Software\b0\fs22\par
Project handoff and usage guide\par
\par
\fs26\b 1. Project Overview\b0\fs22\par
Propentra is a property management SaaS application with a Laravel API backend and a Next.js JavaScript frontend. It supports property portfolios, units, tenants, leases, payments, maintenance, notifications, reports, search, user access, and profile settings.\par
\par
\fs26\b 2. How To Start The Application\b0\fs22\par
Prerequisites: PHP 8.4+, Composer, Node.js, npm, and a configured database.\par
\par
\b Terminal 1 - Backend\b0\par
Open PowerShell in the project root and run:\par
\f1 Set-Location -LiteralPath 'D:\\becky\\Full Stack dev\\Daily-Internship-Projects\\Property Management Software\\backend'\par
php artisan serve --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8000\f0\par
Backend URL: http://localhost:8000\par
API base URL: http://localhost:8000/api/v1\par
\par
\b Terminal 2 - Frontend\b0\par
Open another PowerShell window and run:\par
\f1 Set-Location -LiteralPath 'D:\\becky\\Full Stack dev\\Daily-Internship-Projects\\Property Management Software\\frontend'\par
npm run dev\f0\par
Frontend URL: http://localhost:3000\par
Open: http://localhost:3000/login\par
\par
\b First-time backend setup\b0\par
From the backend directory:\par
\f1 composer install\par
copy .env.example .env\par
php artisan key:generate\par
php artisan migrate\par
php artisan storage:link\f0\par
Configure the database values in backend/.env before running migrations.\par
\par
\fs26\b 3. Main User Workflows\b0\fs22\par
\b Authentication:\b Register or log in at /login. Expired API sessions clear the token and return the user to login.\par
\b Dashboard:\b Shows role-specific statistics, recent properties, payments, maintenance activity, global search, and notifications.\par
\b Properties:\b Create, view, edit, delete, and manage property units. Optional Main, Alternate, and Additional images support JPG, PNG, and WEBP up to 5 MB.\par
\b Units:\b Manage unit number, type, rent, status, bedrooms, bathrooms, area, and property association.\par
\b Tenants:\b View authorized tenant records, create tenant profiles, and open tenant details.\par
\b Leases:\b Create leases, view details, terminate leases, and monitor active or expiring records.\par
\b Payments:\b Record payments, initiate Chapa payments, view payment details, and track status.\par
\b Maintenance:\b Create, assign, complete, view, and delete maintenance requests.\par
\b Search:\b Dashboard search is debounced and returns authorized properties, units, tenants, and leases.\par
\b Notifications:\b The dashboard bell shows unread count, relative timestamps, mark-read, mark-all-read, and view-all actions.\par
\b Reports:\b Reports use a dedicated authorized API endpoint and support optional date-from and date-to filters. Current occupancy and collection-rate visuals use real backend metrics.\par
\b Settings/Profile:\b Update profile name and phone details.\par
\par
\fs26\b 4. Role Access\b0\fs22\par
\b Administrator:\b Platform-wide access, user access management, properties, tenants, leases, payments, maintenance, reports, notifications, settings, and discussion.\par
\b Owner:\b Own properties and related units, tenants, leases, payments, maintenance, reports, notifications, settings, and discussion.\par
\b Manager:\b Assigned properties and related operations, reports, notifications, settings, and discussion.\par
\b Tenant:\b Own lease, payments, maintenance requests, notifications, discussion, profile, and settings.\par
Authorization is enforced on the backend; hidden frontend links are not the security boundary.\par
\par
\fs26\b 5. Security Improvements\b0\fs22\par
- Added property and related-resource authorization to prevent IDOR access.\par
- Replaced unsafe mass-assignment updates with validated fields.\par
- Scoped users, expenses, search, reports, leases, payments, units, tenants, and maintenance.\par
- Added login, registration, search, and payment callback throttling.\par
- Added Sanctum token expiration.\par
- Hardened Chapa callback verification and retry behavior.\par
- Added restricted CORS configuration.\par
- Added safe handling for non-JSON API responses.\par
- Added secure image MIME, extension, and size validation.\par
- Added accessible destructive-action confirmation dialogs.\par
